From 3a4978ebd5a985a5bc557318ec0bc3f06bd768d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:17:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Port RC-Cockpit's IMU module (ICM-20948) to pico-sdk
 hardware_i2c

Replaces the Arduino SparkFun ICM_20948 wrapper classes with the
library's own platform-independent C core (vendored into
cockpit/icm20948/, MIT-licensed, see its README.md), linked to a
small hardware_i2c-based Serif instead of Wire. The sensor-fusion
math itself - complementary filter for pitch/roll, tilt-compensated
magnetometer heading, heading smoothing, slip indicator, the 180
degree mounting correction - is a straight port of imu.cpp.

cockpit_task now calls imuBegin()/imuUpdate() and feeds real pitch/
roll/heading into the PFD, map and pilot-head servo, replacing the
synthetic demo sweep. If the IMU isn't found at startup, it logs via
the existing debug() facility and the loop continues with pitch/
roll/heading at 0 rather than failing, so the rest of the panel and
the servo still come up without the sensor wired.
